# Two reasons, and the second is the one that bites.
#
# Size: venv/ and node_modules/ are the bulk of this directory and are rebuilt
# inside the image anyway.
#
# Secrets and state: anything copied into a layer stays in the image history
# even if a later step deletes it. A baked .env would ship the user's API keys
# to anyone who pulls the image, and a baked projects.db would ship someone
# else's generated projects as the container's starting state.

venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.env
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Generated projects live in a mounted volume, never in the image.
outputs/

# Installed in the jsdeps stage from the lockfile.
scripts/node_modules/

server.log
.DS_Store
.git/
